<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahabad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saujbulagh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahabad is a city in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a>, with a mainly Kurdish population. Formerly called Saujbulagh, it took the name Mahabad in the 1930s. In 1946 it was the capital of the Soviet-backed Republic of Mahabad, the first modern Kurdish republic, which collapsed when Iranian troops returned in December 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahabad.jpg" alt="Mahabad" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simko at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahabad-Dec_2006.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
